# Frontend (React SPA)

Stack: React + TS strict + Tailwind. Data via REST /api only (axios).

Layers: Page → Component → hook; HTTP in api/; DTO in types/

Map↔backend: Page≈Controller | hook/api≈Service | types≈Resource | UI checks≈FormRequest | auth later≈Policy

## Layout
- Pages/: screen state, effects, api orchestration
- Components/: UI + callbacks only
- hooks/: reusable logic (useX)
- api/: thin HTTP wrappers on shared client
- types/: API DTOs / unions; no runtime logic
- lib/themes.ts: theme registry (accent palettes)
- hooks/useActiveTheme.ts: active tab index → theme

## Themes
UI is theme-driven. Active tab index maps to a theme in `lib/themes.ts` (cycles).
Page applies `theme.vars` + `data-theme` on the shell; Components consume `var(--theme-*)` only — no hard-coded accents per theme.

### Files
- `types/theme.ts` — `ThemeId`, `ThemeCssVars`, `AppTheme`, tab chip types
- `lib/themes.ts` — `THEMES[]`, `themeAt`, `themeIndexForTab`
- `hooks/useActiveTheme.ts` — resolve theme from tabs + activeTabId
- `resources/css/app.css` — defaults for `--theme-*`, shell/panel/card helpers

### Add a new theme
1. Add id to `ThemeId` in `types/theme.ts`
2. Append full `AppTheme` to `THEMES` in `lib/themes.ts` (every key in `ThemeCssVars` + `tab` chip)
3. Keep order = tab color cycle; do not leave gaps or partial vars

### Add a themed UI token / element
1. Add the CSS var to `ThemeCssVars` in `types/theme.ts`
2. Set a value in **every** theme in `THEMES` (required — no theme may omit it)
3. Add `:root` fallback in `app.css` if needed
4. Use only `var(--theme-…)` in Components/CSS — never a one-off accent hex in JSX for themeable surfaces

### Must (themes)
- New accent/surface color → new `--theme-*` in the type + all themes
- Tab chips use `theme.tab` utilities; shell/surfaces use CSS vars
- Theme switch must recolor background, panel, sidebar, cards, buttons, orbs

## Must
- Typed props/state. Prefer explicit types over any.
- Components: no axios/fetch. Call via props or Page/hook.
- api/: no JSX. One module per resource (tabs, notes…).
- Errors: surface to user; never empty catch.
- Names: PascalCase components/files; camelCase fns; useX hooks.
- Styles: Tailwind + theme CSS vars (`app.css` / `lib/themes.ts`). Keep UI lean.
- Keep Page thin: extract repeated logic to hooks.

## Never
- Business/HTTP logic inside presentational Components
- Duplicate API calls / types across files
- Dead code, console noise in prod paths, untyped any without reason
- Hard-coded theme accents in Components (bypass `--theme-*`)
- Partial theme definitions (missing vars in some themes)
